  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new undoable command, `VouchModelFidelity { model, by }`, clears the \"fidelity unknown\" mark of one model. It also clears the mark of each stock that is copied straight from that model.\n- The command is one labelled undo step. The label names the person who vouched. Undo puts each mark back.\n- The command refuses by name:\n  - a model with a recorded coarse chord (#864);\n  - an incomplete model (#1610);\n  - a model that is not marked;\n  - a name that is not a model;\n  - an empty name of the person who vouches.\n- A new component, `FidelityVouched { by, rev }`, records who vouched. The record is valid only while the model has the same geometry revision and no fidelity flag.\n- The project file keeps the record in the optional key `fidelity_vouched` of the model row. There is no project version step.\n- The MCP tool `vouch_model_fidelity { model, by }` runs the same command. `get_job` shows `models[].fidelity_vouched`. A script uses the tool through `cam.call`.\n- The model page shows a name field and the button \"Vouch for this mesh\" below the \"Fidelity unknown\" line. A vouched model shows who vouched.\n\n## Cause\n\nSince project v59, each mesh of an older project without a recorded chord loads as \"fidelity unknown\" (#1056). The gate refuses its operations until a re-import. A model whose source file is gone, or whose mesh is exact, had no other path to a post.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/vouch_fidelity_mcp.rs`\n  - `a_vouched_model_posts_and_its_undo_is_refused_again`: the post refuses, the tool vouches, the post writes a file, undo refuses again, redo passes again.\n  - `the_tool_refuses_by_name_and_enters_no_history`\n- `crates/app/tests/vouch_fidelity.rs`\n  - `a_vouched_model_passes_the_gate_and_its_undo_is_refused_again`\n  - `a_recorded_coarse_chord_is_never_vouched_away`\n  - `every_other_bad_input_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `the_record_speaks_only_for_the_facets_it_was_given_for`\n  - `the_vouch_rides_the_project_file`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/model_vouch.rs`\n  - `model_page_vouches_for_an_unknown_mesh_and_undo_brings_the_row_back`\n\nRed before the change: `a_vouched_model_posts_and_its_undo_is_refused_again` failed on unchanged `upstream/main` (`e048b103c`) at the assert \"the tool is listed\". The asserts before it passed: the gate and the post refused the model by name.\n\nMutation results (each guard removed, pins run, guard restored):\n\n| Guard removed | Result | Failing pin |\n|---|---|---|\n| a recorded coarse chord is refused | red | `a_recorded_coarse_chord_is_never_vouched_away` |\n| an incomplete mesh is refused | red | `every_other_bad_input_is_refused_by_name` |\n| only stock copies with the unknown mark are cleared | red | `a_recorded_coarse_chord_is_never_vouched_away` |\n| a name that is not a model is refused | red | `every_other_bad_input_is_refused_by_name` |\n| an empty name of the person is refused | red | `every_other_bad_input_is_refused_by_name` |\n| the record is silent for other facets (`rev`) | red | `the_record_speaks_only_for_the_facets_it_was_given_for` |\n| the record is silent beside a flag | red | `the_record_speaks_only_for_the_facets_it_was_given_for` |\n| the loader refuses a vouch beside a flag | red | `the_vouch_rides_the_project_file` |\n| undo puts the mark back | red | `a_vouched_model_passes_the_gate_and_its_undo_is_refused_again` |\n\nAll pins are green with each guard restored.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on `beb3a91cb`: 339 steps, 0 failed (the app suites that the diff selects, the `camcraft-ui` lib tests and 16 ui suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. The gate and clippy ran with an empty `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, because the shared sccache server did not answer compile requests.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The name field was not typed into through the keyboard. The UI pin sets the draft and clicks the button.\n- A fixture of unknown fidelity was not vouched in a test. A fixture is a model, so the command accepts it.\n- A stock copy whose source model is deleted is not covered. The command takes a model name.\n- No pixel snapshot was made. The app window was not opened by hand.\n- The row for `vouch_model_fidelity` in `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` is not in this PR. The session could not write to that path. The tool description in `crates/app/src/mcp/vouch_tools.rs` has the facts for the row. A session that can write process files must add the row.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2024 changes `crates/app/src/model_fidelity.rs` and `crates/app/src/mesh_open.rs` (`coarse_source`, `adopt_copies`, `hole_of`, `set`). This PR changes two doc comments in `model_fidelity.rs` and no function there. It touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2792, #2773, #2716, #2678, #2554 and #2149 add rows to the module lists in `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs` or `crates/app/src/commands/mod.rs`. This PR adds one row to each list. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1339-vouch-fidelity.md`.\n\nChangelog: Model page and MCP: a model marked \"fidelity unknown\" (a project saved before v59) can be vouched for by a named person (`VouchModelFidelity`, `vouch_model_fidelity`), so its operations post again without a re-import; undo puts the mark back.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1339\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
